## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end data export pipelines, PII masking, ordering guarantees, and resiliency across regions, using realistic components (Kafka, Spark, REST API) and failure modes.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end data pipelines (Kafka, Spark, REST API)
- Data masking and PII handling
- Exactly-once or idempotent retries with replay-safe semantics
- Cross-region replication and chaos testing
- Validation via replayable event stores and SLA checks

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: seed events, validate masking, simulate 503s, verify idempotency
const seedEvents = genSyntheticTransactions(1000);
publishToKafka(seedEvents);
const masked = consumeKafkaTopic('transactions.masked');
assert(masked.every(e => e.piI === null));
const payloads = buildPayloadsForPartner(masked);
mockPartnerApi.setBehavior({ failRate: 0.2 });
sendToPartner(payloads);
assert(retryStore.isIdempotent());
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test late-arriving events affecting ordering?
- How would you approach data quality checks for transformed analytics downstream?

